\* TIER-2 CERT LEG — Mutation 3 (AttemptFencing = FALSE). EXPECT: VIOLATION.
\* ***THIS IS THE BINDING LEG OF THE BOUND-SEARCH.***
\*
\* Designed harm: no activation_attempt_id fencing => a stale INITIAL commit violates
\* `ServiceSafety`/`TupleSafety`. This mutation has NEVER fired at the large bounds
\* (~380M states, `verdict=INCONCLUSIVE`, §6) — it is deep in a large space, not a doubt
\* about the harm (the randomized sim catches the same sabotage at median 187 steps, and
\* Mut3Fast exists precisely because smaller sound bounds make it shallow).
\*
\* The ratified search procedure (PROJECT_STATE §6): ITERATE `MaxMsgs` UPWARD until this
\* leg fires. The bound that certifies is the smallest at which THIS leg fires AND the
\* other three mutations still fire AND both baselines still reach conclusive verdicts.
\* `MaxMsgs` is a bound, never model logic (rules 6 and 9).
\*
\* @MAXMSGS@ is substituted by the tlc-cert workflow from the `cert_msgs` dispatch input.
SPECIFICATION Spec

SYMMETRY Sym

CONSTRAINT
CertConstraint

CONSTANTS
Stages = {s1, s2}
MaxEpoch = 1
MaxRId = 1
MaxAttempt = 2
MaxPos = 1
MaxCrashes = 1
MaxMsgs = @MAXMSGS@
EnableUnservable = TRUE
ResetTruncates = TRUE
AttemptFencing = FALSE
AbortGuardEnabled = TRUE

INVARIANTS
Inv
